                <h2 id="titles">Professional Overview</h2>

                <p>Throughout my <b>9-year career</b> across studios from indie to AAA, I have consistently occupied a central, cross-disciplinary role – gravitating toward the tools, pipelines, and workflows that empower how teams create. The majority of my work has been in <b>Unity</b>, specialising in the editors, asset pipelines, and authoring tools developers depend on every day.</p>

                <p>My technical contributions span <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/tools" class="textual-link" target="_blank">authoring tools<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>, <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/systems" class="textual-link" target="_blank">systems<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>, <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/backend" class="textual-link" target="_blank">backend infrastructure<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>, <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/multiplayer" class="textual-link" target="_blank">multiplayer<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>, <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/gameplay" class="textual-link" target="_blank">gameplay<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>, and <b><a href="@explicitBaseUri/portfolio/technicalart" class="textual-link" target="_blank">technical art<SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#icon-external-link" class="external-link-icon" /></a></b>. This breadth lets me evaluate various complex cross-system technology stacks and articulate technical concepts clearly to any audience from engineers to executives, and credibly collaborate with counterparts across diverse engineering teams – a foundation I now bring to product leadership.</p>

                <h3>Tools, Workflows & UX</h3>

                <p>As a Tools Programmer, I think of myself as a <b>"Workflow Engineer"</b>, responsible not just for technical delivery but for the full experience of the people using what I build.</p>

                <p>My approach is <b>product-focused</b>. I gather requirements directly from artists, designers, and producers, design solutions alongside them, and iterate against their feedback. I am experienced in scoping, prioritising, facilitating cross-team communication, and presenting deliverables to stakeholders. I approach prioritisation by balancing user impact, technical feasibility, and business goals – making trade-offs transparent and driving alignment before work begins.</p>

                <p>I take knowledge sharing seriously. A tool no one knows how to use is a tool that fails, so I regularly produce tutorial videos and documentation for end users alongside technical docs for other engineers. Facilitating that feedback loop is something I consider a core part of the job, not an afterthought.</p>

                <p>I also believe in teaching teams what Unity already offers because often the best solution is helping developers get more out of existing tools, rather than building new ones. Knowing the <b>Unity Engine</b> deeply enough to make that call is a skill I have developed over decade using Unity, with my first Unity version being <b>Unity 4.1.2</b> in <b>2013</b>.</p>

